==English==

===Etymology===
Earliest uses (late 16th c.) "to spend recklessly or prodigiously", also "to scatter over a wide area". Of {{unk|en|title=unknown origin}}. Perhaps a {{blend|en|scatter|wander|nocap=1}}.

Compare {{cog|da|skvætte}} {{q|rare}}/{{m|da|skvatte|t=to splash}} (nominalised: {{m|da|skvæt}}), {{cog|is|skvetta|t=to squirt}}, {{cog|sv|skvätta|t=to splash}}, {{cog|nb|skvette}}.<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|squander}}</ref>

